=== EXIT DECISION HIERARCHY (EVALUATE IN STRICT ORDER) ===

1) SESSION & TIME-DECAY GATE (Overnight / Stale Trade Filter):
   - An M15 scalp thesis is valid for 1 to 4 bars (15–60 min).
   - If SESSION transitions into LOW_LIQUIDITY_DEADZONE or ASIAN_SESSION_CHOP (post-NY close), OR if
     Time in Trade >= 60 min and {pnl_atr} < +0.30:
     * Answer CLOSE if the trade is stalled, chopping near entry/EMA20, or underwater once the forming bar
       bounces toward its open/mean. Do NOT carry passive losers or stalled scalps across the NY close into
       overnight illiquidity.

2) CLOSED-BAR THESIS INVALIDATION (Cut Losers Early on Closed Structure — NEVER on Forming Spikes):
   - Evaluate the LAST CLOSED M15 BAR ({last_c}) first:
     * Answer CLOSE immediately if the last CLOSED M15 candle closed beyond {invalid_level_price} against your
       side, OR closed on the losing side of M15 EMA20 + VWAP with opposing CVD ({cvd_label} / {cvd_slope}),
       OR if 2 consecutive closed M15 bars made lower closes (for LONG) / higher closes (for SHORT) below entry.
   - ANTI-PANIC / NO INTRABAR CAPITULATION RULE (Critical when {pnl_atr} < 0):
     * NEVER trigger a loss exit solely because the LIVE FORMING BAR spikes through {invalid_level_price} or
       EMA20 intrabar. Sudden intrabar flushes (especially when {pnl_atr} <= -0.80 M15_ATR or near the +/-2 ATR
       band) are liquidity sweeps that mean-revert before the 15-minute bar closes.
     * During a sharp adverse forming-bar spike, answer HOLD and wait for the M15 candle close or a snap-back
       toward the forming bar's open/EMA20. Only exit intrabar on the losing side if catastrophic continuation
       pushes beyond -1.25 M15_ATR AFTER a closed M15 bar has ALREADY broken structure.

3) PROACTIVE TARGET HARVESTING (Close Into Strength at Walls):
   - When in profit ({pnl_atr} >= +0.35 M15_ATR) and price reaches within 0.12 M15_ATR of {next_wall_price}
     ({next_wall_label} — especially Call Wall #1, Put Wall #1, VAH/VAL, or Session High/Low):
     * Answer CLOSE INTO STRENGTH while live price is pressing the wall. Do NOT wait for a reversal wick or
       for the forming bar to pull back away from the level before closing.

4) RATCHETING PROFIT PROTECTION (Giveback Guardrails):
   - Mid-Tier Winner (MFE {mfe_atr} >= +0.45 M15_ATR):
     * Answer CLOSE if {giveback_pct}% >= 40% AND either live price crosses back against M15 EMA20 or CVD slope
       ({cvd_slope}) turns against the trade.
   - Early Winner (MFE {mfe_atr} between +0.30 and +0.44 M15_ATR):
     * Do not let a green scalp turn into a deep red hold. If {giveback_pct}% >= 70% and the last closed M15
       bar failed to make progress in your direction, answer CLOSE near breakeven.
   - Extended Runner (MFE {mfe_atr} >= +0.85 M15_ATR):
     * Answer CLOSE if {giveback_pct}% >= 30% or immediately upon touching {next_wall_price}.

